@startuml implementation-issue-states
' cumin works - states of an implementation issue.
' A state is a label on GitHub. Each arrow is one transition. Its first line names the step of cumin
' that makes it (with the row of issue-states.md), and the second line says what happened.
' One step can have several arrows. I9 and I11 change no state; they are notes.
' Render: run scripts/render-diagrams.sh at the root of the repository.

hide empty description

state "Draft\n(no status label)" as Draft
state "cumin/status/ready" as Ready
state "cumin/status/implementing" as Implementing
state "cumin/status/awaiting-checks" as Checks
state "cumin/status/reviewing" as Reviewing
state "cumin/status/awaiting-owner-review" as OwnerReview
state "cumin/status/awaiting-owner-decision" as Decision

[*] --> Draft : the Planner or the Owner\ncreates a sub-issue
Draft --> Ready : the Owner checks it,\nadds cumin/status/ready
Ready --> Implementing : I1 request the implementation:\nthe Implementer is asked
Implementing --> Checks : I2 check the finished work:\nthe pull request is verified,\nthe checks run
Implementing --> Decision : I2 check the finished work:\nblocked, the pull request failed the check,\nor two abnormal ends
Checks --> Reviewing : I3 request the review:\nthe required checks passed
Checks --> Implementing : I4 request a check fix:\na required check failed
Checks --> Decision : I4 request a check fix:\nthe fix requests are at the limit
Checks --> Implementing : I14 request a conflict resolution:\nthe pull request conflicts
Checks --> Decision : I15 stop for missing checks:\nthe required checks do not report in time
Reviewing --> Implementing : check the review (I5):\nchanges requested
Reviewing --> [*] : check the review (I6):\napproved, risk/low, cumin merges
Reviewing --> OwnerReview : check the review (I7):\napproved, risk/medium or risk/high,\nthe Owner decides the merge
Reviewing --> Decision : check the review (I8):\ncomments left at the round limit,\nthe Reviewer explains the cause
Reviewing --> Decision : check the review (I10):\nthe Reviewer returned blocked,\nor left no review twice
Reviewing --> Checks : check the review (no row today):\nthe head commit moved, or a required\ncheck does not pass
OwnerReview --> [*] : I12 merge on the Owner's approval:\nthe Owner approved the head commit,\ncumin merges
OwnerReview --> Implementing : I13 request a response to the Owner's review:\nthe Owner requested changes
OwnerReview --> Implementing : I14 request a conflict resolution:\nthe pull request conflicts
OwnerReview --> Ready : the Owner sends it back\n(comment, cumin/status/ready again)
Decision --> Ready : the Owner answers,\nadds cumin/status/ready again

note "I11 copy the labels to the pull request:\nin every state, no transition." as I11
note "I9 write the follow-up note:\nafter every merge, no transition." as I9

legend right
  First line of an arrow: the step of cumin (a row of issue-states.md).
  Second line: what happened (the transition).
  An arrow without a row: the Owner, or the Planner, acts.
  "check the review" is one step after a Reviewer run; today it is five rows.
endlegend

@enduml
